%rec: default
#FIELDS: id owner towards role at window performed absent
#
# An Obligation is a duty pointing either at another Townsperson or at the town.
# It is the only thing this simulation propagates: when someone goes Absent their
# Obligations are voided, offered to whoever they pointed at, then to anyone whose
# Role suits — and if nobody has the free hours, they go Unmet for good.
#
#   owner      who currently owes it
#   towards    who it is owed to; leave empty when it is owed to the town.
#              Reassignment tries this person first.
#   role       who may inherit it once the person above has been tried. Leave
#              empty and the duty dies with its holder.
#   window     HH:MM-HH:MM. Must not collide with the owner's Routine — the
#              Schedule resolves Obligations into the hours the Routine leaves free.
#   performed  what a watcher sees when it happens
#   absent     what the town looks like when it does not
#
# This is the town's economy, and it is the whole of it. Food is produced by
# four people — Elias grows it, Jorin keeps the animals, Bram works the river,
# Martin grinds what Elias brings him — and leaves them along two routes: to
# Greta, who cooks it, and to Hilde, who sells it. Those two then push it back
# out to everyone who cannot stop working to come and get it. Otto keeps the
# metal of all of it working and Marta keeps the buildings up, so both of them
# touch every other trade without producing anything themselves. Aldren
# produces nothing and is owed nothing, and touches everyone.
#
# Four of the nine are Role farmer, so a delivery that dies with one of them can
# land on any of the other three — provided one of them still has the hours. The
# smith's duties and the carpenter's can go to nobody at all: each is the only
# one of their Role in town, which is why losing either is permanent in a way
# that losing a farmer is not.

id: vegetables_to_the_inn
owner: elias
towards: greta
role: farmer
at: inn
window: 11:00-12:00
performed: carries a full basket in through the inn door and leaves it by the counter
absent: The inn's kitchen bench stays bare and the stew is thinner every day

id: grain_to_the_mill
owner: elias
towards: martin
role: farmer
at: mill
window: 16:00-17:00
performed: hauls a grain sack the length of the road and drops it by the chute
absent: The chute stands empty and the millstones are not turned at all

id: flour_to_the_inn
owner: martin
towards: greta
role: farmer
at: inn
window: 18:00-19:00
performed: carries two flour sacks to the inn and stacks them inside the door
absent: There is no flour in the inn and no bread on the tables

id: repair_the_farm_tools
owner: otto
towards: elias
role: smith
at: blacksmith
window: 12:00-13:00
performed: works a hoe blade flat on the anvil while the farmer waits
absent: The farm tools go unmended and the rows are worked half as fast

id: repair_the_carpenters_tools
owner: otto
towards: marta
role: smith
at: carpenter_workshop
window: 17:00-18:00
performed: carries a mended saw down to the workshop and tries it on a board
absent: A blunt saw hangs on the workshop wall and nothing gets cut straight

id: repair_the_mill
owner: marta
towards: martin
role: builder
at: mill
window: 11:00-12:00
performed: works on the waterwheel with boards under one arm until it stops squealing
absent: The waterwheel screams all day and the mill runs slower each week

id: repair_the_inn
owner: marta
towards: greta
role: builder
at: inn
window: 17:00-18:00
performed: rights a broken chair in the common room and hammers it back together
absent: Broken chairs pile up by the inn door and nobody sits at the far table

id: feed_the_town
owner: greta
role: trader
at: inn
window: 12:00-13:00
performed: carries bowls out to every table without being asked for them
absent: The common room is dark at noon and people eat standing in their own houses

id: hold_the_service
owner: aldren
role: authority
at: church
window: 07:00-09:00
performed: rings the bell, then reads to whoever came
absent: The bell does not ring, and by the second morning nobody comes to hear it

id: bless_the_fields
owner: aldren
role: authority
at: vegetable_field
window: 11:00-13:00
performed: walks the crop rows with a hand raised over them
absent: The rows go unblessed, and the farmer works them like a man who expects nothing

# The morning goods. Three producers walk into town between six and noon — the
# herd, the river and the fields — and each of them splits what they carry
# between the inn, which feeds people, and the stall, which sells to them. Two
# destinations for every producer is what makes the damage legible: kill a
# producer and both the kitchen and the counter go short, and the player can see
# which one he took by what stops arriving where.

id: milk_to_the_inn
owner: jorin
towards: greta
role: farmer
at: inn
window: 06:00-07:00
performed: sets two covered pails inside the inn door while the kitchen is still dark
absent: No milk reaches the inn, and what is served at noon is water and salt

id: eggs_to_the_market
owner: jorin
towards: hilde
role: farmer
at: market_stall
window: 08:00-09:00
performed: unpacks eggs onto the stall one at a time, turning each one over first
absent: The egg baskets on the stall stay stacked and empty all morning

id: fish_to_the_inn
owner: bram
towards: greta
role: farmer
at: inn
window: 10:00-11:00
performed: carries the morning's catch up from the river and hands it over at the kitchen door
absent: Nothing comes up from the river, and the inn serves the same pot it served yesterday

id: fish_to_the_market
owner: bram
towards: hilde
role: farmer
at: market_stall
window: 11:00-12:00
performed: lays what the inn did not take out on the stall and stands back from the smell
absent: The slab at the end of the stall stays dry, and people stop walking past it

id: vegetables_to_the_market
owner: elias
towards: hilde
role: farmer
at: market_stall
window: 10:00-11:00
performed: wheels a barrow up from the field and tips greens onto the stall unsorted
absent: There are no greens on the stall, and the people who cannot farm go without them

# What the market sends back out. Hilde's counter is only half the trade: the
# people who cannot leave their work — the smith at his fire, the priest with
# the poor to feed — are reached by her walking to them.

id: the_rounds
owner: hilde
towards: otto
role: trader
at: blacksmith
window: 17:00-18:00
performed: comes to the forge door with a basket and leaves with it lighter
absent: Nobody brings the smith anything, and he works through the evening on nothing

id: the_tithe_basket
owner: hilde
towards: aldren
role: trader
at: church
window: 18:00-19:00
performed: carries what did not sell down to the church and sets it inside the door
absent: There is nothing at the church door to hand out, and the priest stops looking for it

# The craft side of the new trade. The smith keeps the river working and the
# carpenter keeps the stall standing — the same pattern as the mill and the inn,
# extended to the two trades the town has just gained.

id: mend_the_hooks
owner: otto
towards: bram
role: smith
at: blacksmith
window: 18:00-19:00
performed: straightens a handful of hooks one after another while the fisherman waits
absent: The hooks stay bent, and less comes out of the river every week

id: repair_the_market_stall
owner: marta
towards: hilde
role: builder
at: market_stall
window: 12:00-13:00
performed: puts a shoulder under the stall's awning and nails the brace back on
absent: The stall leans further each day, and in the end she sells off the ground

# Private Actions. These are only carried out when nobody outside the whitelist
# can see. A group secret is a whitelist with more than one name on it — watching
# who is permitted to be present is itself informative.

id: the_grave_visit
owner: elias
at: childs_grave
window: 20:00-21:00
private: true
witness: aldren
performed: sets flowers on a small grave and stands over it without speaking
absent: A grave at the back of the cemetery goes untended and the flowers dry out

id: the_sleepwalk
owner: martin
at: quiet_riverbank
window: 02:00-03:00
private: true
performed: walks out of the mill in the dark, stands at the water, and walks back
absent: Nothing happens at the river at night, and nobody would have known to miss it

id: watering_the_ale
owner: greta
at: inn_cellar
window: 22:00-23:00
private: true
performed: carries a bucket down to the cellar and stands a long while at the barrel
absent: The ale is honest, the barrels run out early, and the takings do not cover the week

id: collecting_the_scrap
owner: otto
at: smith_storage
window: 19:00-20:00
private: true
performed: waits until the forge is empty, then gathers the iron offcuts into the back room
absent: Iron scrap lies where it fell around the anvil and slowly rusts

id: carving_the_toy
owner: marta
at: carpenter_bedroom
window: 21:00-22:00
private: true
performed: sits at the bench with one small piece of wood and does not light the lamp for it
absent: The drawer by the bed stays shut and nothing new is put in it

id: rehearsing_the_sermon
owner: aldren
at: priest_study
window: 20:00-22:00
private: true
performed: paces the study reading the same page aloud until it sounds meant
absent: Sunday's words come out flat and the congregation cannot say why
